# A jj workspace has no .git, so a plain `use flake` copies the whole folder into the Nix store,
# target/ included, at each reload: evaluate a copy of flake.nix and flake.lock alone, as
# scripts/dev-shell does (.agents/wiki/parallel-workspaces.md). The copy is read-only, so Nix
# must not write a lock update back.
use flake "path:$(scripts/dev-shell --flake)" --no-write-lock-file
